    "title": "Edward F. Nickless, 73, Passes Away Surrounded by Family",
    "text": "Edward F. Nickless | Curley Funeral Home\nEdward F. Nickless | Curley Funeral Home\nHe is survived by brothers Bill (Sandy), Bob (Kathy), Jerry (Diane), Jack (Lynn) Nickless, and Rita (John) Ulrich, as well as brothers-in-law Tom (Lynne) Braun, Tim (Jean) Braun, Jeanne (Ray) Venegas, Terry (Janice) Braun, and many nieces and nephews. Edward was preceded in death by his parents William and Rita Nickless, and his in-laws, Tom and Carole Braun.\nEdward was a proud member of Local 143 Operating Engineers, serving the Chicago Public Schools for 40 years. In lieu of flowers, donations may be made to the Pulmonary Fibrosis Foundation in Ed’s name.\nVisitation will be held on Tuesday, July 29, 2025, from 3:00 p.m. until 8:00 p.m. at Curley Funeral Home, located at 6116 W. 111th St., Chicago Ridge. The funeral mass will take place at 11:00 a.m. on Wednesday, July 30, 2025, at Incarnation Catholic Church, 5757 W. 127th Street in Crestwood. For more information about the funeral arrangements, please visit the Curley Funeral Home website.\nClick here to read the original obituary.",
